WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.582
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:09.443
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:17.271
Unit thirty-five: Dependent Prepositions. Today you will use the correct preposition after verbs and adjectives.

4
00:00:17.571 --> 00:00:20.351
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.510
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.398
Depend on.

7
00:00:27.383 --> 00:00:29.638
Depend on means to be decided by.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.785
It depends on the weather.

9
00:00:32.383 --> 00:00:35.001
Your turn. Say: Depend on.

10
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:38.949
Depend on.

11
00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:40.568
Succeed in.

12
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:43.676
Succeed in means to achieve a goal.

13
00:00:44.283 --> 00:00:46.062
She succeeded in passing.

14
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.175
Your turn. Say: Succeed in.

15
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.313
Succeed in.

16
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.086
Believe in.

17
00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:59.221
Believe in means to trust that something exists or is good.

18
00:00:59.817 --> 00:01:01.421
I believe in hard work.

19
00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:04.704
Your turn. Say: Believe in.

20
00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.661
Believe in.

21
00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:10.778
Apologise for.

22
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:14.421
Apologise for means to say sorry about.

23
00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:16.912
I apologise for being late.

24
00:01:17.517 --> 00:01:20.355
Your turn. Say: Apologise for.

25
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.735
Apologise for.

26
00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:26.519
Worry about.

27
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:29.725
Worry about means to feel anxious.

28
00:01:30.317 --> 00:01:31.538
Don't worry about it.

29
00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.826
Your turn. Say: Worry about.

30
00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:38.726
Worry about.

31
00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:40.403
Agree with.

32
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:43.823
Agree with means to have the same opinion.

33
00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:45.650
I agree with you.

34
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.809
Your turn. Say: Agree with.

35
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:52.772
Agree with.

36
00:01:53.517 --> 00:01:54.564
Different from.

37
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.793
Different from means not the same as.

38
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:00.011
Cats are different from dogs.

39
00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:03.362
Your turn. Say: Different from.

40
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.201
Different from.

41
00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.021
Result in.

42
00:02:10.017 --> 00:02:11.830
Result in means to cause.

43
00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:14.451
Hard work results in success.

44
00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:17.900
Your turn. Say: Result in.

45
00:02:20.733 --> 00:02:21.932
Result in.

46
00:02:22.733 --> 00:02:26.465
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.317 --> 00:02:30.361
Visal, make two sentences with fixed prepositions.

48
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:42.229
I believe in hard work, and I always apologise for mistakes. Many verbs and adjectives are followed by a fixed preposition that we must learn.

49
00:02:43.317 --> 00:02:44.608
How do we learn them?

50
00:02:45.717 --> 00:02:58.458
Learn the whole phrase: depend on, succeed in, agree with, worry about. After the preposition we use a noun or an -ing form: She succeeded in passing the exam.

51
00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.271
Any common mistakes?

52
00:03:02.383 --> 00:03:15.789
Different from, not different than in formal writing. Agree with a person, agree on a plan. And never add a preposition after discuss: We discussed the problem, not discussed about.

53
00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:18.376
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:24.711
Grammar focus: Dependent prepositions: verb and adjective plus preposition.

55
00:03:25.011 --> 00:03:26.279
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.983 --> 00:03:28.484
It depends on the weather.

57
00:03:29.383 --> 00:03:31.580
She succeeded in passing the exam.

58
00:03:32.483 --> 00:03:34.425
I apologise for being late.

59
00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:44.741
Learn verbs with their prepositions: depend on, succeed in, believe in, apologise for, worry about, agree with, different from, result in. Then use a noun or -ing.

60
00:03:45.483 --> 00:03:48.797
Be careful! Don't say: We discussed about it.

61
00:03:50.733 --> 00:03:52.559
Say: We discussed it.

62
00:03:52.859 --> 00:03:54.870
Discuss takes no preposition.

63
00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.354
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.528
Fixed Partners.

65
00:04:00.828 --> 00:04:02.374
I believe in hard work.

66
00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.749
My brother succeeded in passing the exam.

67
00:04:06.733 --> 00:04:08.686
I apologise for being late.

68
00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.165
It depends on the weather.

69
00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.398
Hard work often results in success.

70
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.281
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:20.117 --> 00:04:21.489
I agree blank you.

72
00:04:21.789 --> 00:04:24.781
A, with. B, to. C, on.

73
00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:30.147
The answer is A: with.

74
00:04:31.283 --> 00:04:33.689
She succeeded blank passing the test.

75
00:04:33.989 --> 00:04:37.027
A, in. B, at. C, for.

76
00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.032
The answer is A: in.

77
00:04:43.183 --> 00:04:44.846
It depends blank the weather.

78
00:04:45.146 --> 00:04:48.057
A, of. B, on. C, from.

79
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.553
The answer is B: on.

80
00:04:54.717 --> 00:04:55.996
Which is correct?

81
00:04:56.296 --> 00:05:02.446
A, We discussed about the plan.. B, We discussed the plan.. C, We discussed on the plan..

82
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.278
The answer is B: We discussed the plan..

83
00:05:09.417 --> 00:05:12.821
According to the reading, what does hard work result in?

84
00:05:13.121 --> 00:05:16.844
A, success. B, trouble. C, delay.

85
00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.458
The answer is A: success.

86
00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:26.749
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:27.583 --> 00:05:31.290
Write two sentences with verbs followed by fixed prepositions.

88
00:05:40.083 --> 00:05:41.514
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.814 --> 00:05:53.374
I worry about the exam, but I believe in my preparation. I also apologise for any mistakes, because I am learning. These verbs always take fixed prepositions.

90
00:05:53.674 --> 00:05:56.115
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:57.017 --> 00:06:03.674
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and dependent prepositions: verb and adjective plus preposition.

92
00:06:03.974 --> 00:06:07.974
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

93
00:06:08.274 --> 00:06:11.715
See you in Unit thirty-six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:12.015 --> 00:06:14.795
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

